      "Toussaint Louverture, a formerly enslaved man, emerged as the leading general. He fought off Spanish and British forces and by 1801 controlled the whole island, issuing a constitution that made him governor for life while keeping the colony nominally French. In 1802 Napoleon Bonaparte sent a large army under General Leclerc to restore French control, and in the same year France reinstated slavery in its other colonies. Toussaint was seized and deported to France, where he died in prison in 1803.",
